[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/4306651250","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/181146#issuecomment-4306651250","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/181146","id":4306651250,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z88AAAABALJIcg","user":{"login":"GSumanth109","id":37910951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3OTEwOTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37910951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109","html_url":"https://github.com/GSumanth109","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-23T18:01:08Z","updated_at":"2026-04-23T18:01:08Z","body":"I reproduced the bug on current main. The root cause is in `AutogradFunctionApplyVariable.rewire_bwd_graph_outputs` in `torch/_dynamo/variables/higher_order_ops.py`, when the same tensor is passed to multiple positional slots of `apply()`, the loop over `orig_fwd_args` blindly overwrites `outer_fwd_proxy_to_bwd_node[fwd_proxy]` on each iteration instead of accumulating, so only the last slot's backward contribution survives.\n\nFix: extract `fwd_proxy = fwd_arg.proxy` and accumulate via `bwd_graph.call_function(operator.add, ...)` when the proxy is already mapped to a non-None node, and guard the None assignment with `if fwd_proxy not in outer_fwd_proxy_to_bwd_node` to prevent None from overwriting a real gradient.\n\nAll 8 permutations of the 3-alias case pass, and the full `AutogradFunctionTests` suite passes with no regressions. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/4306651250/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/4313008325","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/181146#issuecomment-4313008325","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/181146","id":4313008325,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z88AAAABARNIxQ","user":{"login":"GSumanth109","id":37910951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3OTEwOTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37910951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109","html_url":"https://github.com/GSumanth109","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GSumanth109/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-24T12:08:02Z","updated_at":"2026-04-24T12:08:02Z","body":"Happy to submit a PR for this if that would be helpful. I just wanted to check before opening one.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions"